=> The outbreak count (2 + 2) sits ONLY on the two header rows; the four
   species rows carry animal counts and '-' for New outbreaks. Summing the
   'New outbreaks' column over every row therefore does NOT double-count,
   because detail rows contribute NaN, not a repeated total. Summing
   animal counts over every row likewise does not double-count, because
   header rows contribute NaN. The real hazard is the opposite one:
   converting '-' to 0 before aggregating, which would fabricate zeros.

