D. INTERNAL CONSISTENCY OF THE ANIMAL-COUNT FIELDS
==============================================================================
                             check  comparable_rows  violations  pct
               Cases > Susceptible              508           4  0.8
                    Deaths > Cases              532           5  0.9
              Deaths > Susceptible              529           4  0.8
      Killed & disposed of > Cases              530          65 12.3
Killed & disposed of > Susceptible              508           1  0.2

=> 'Killed and disposed of' exceeds 'Cases' on 12% of comparable rows.
   That is expected, not an error: culling removes healthy in-contact
   birds as a CONTROL measure. It is a response indicator, not a measure
   of disease. The small number of Cases>Susceptible and Deaths>Cases
   violations are genuine source-data inconsistencies and are retained
   and flagged rather than corrected.

